{{{{{1<noinclude>|Ability data</noinclude>}}}|Undertow|{{{2|}}}|{{{3|}}}|{{{4|}}}|{{{5|}}}
|champion     = Olaf
|skill        = Q
|icon         = Undertow.png
|blurb        = {{sbc|Active:}} {{ci|Olaf}} throws an axe to the target location that deals {{as|physical damage}} to enemies it passes through, briefly {{tip|slow|slowing}} them based on distance travelled. Enemy {{tip|champions}} hit also have {{sti|armor penetration|{{as|reduced armor}}}} for a few seconds.
|blurb2      = The axe remains in place during the cooldown, and '''Olaf''' can pick up the axe to reduce the {{sti|cd|'''total''' cooldown}}.
|description = {{sbc|Active:}} '''Olaf''' throws an axe to the target location that deals {{as|physical damage}} to enemies it passes through and {{tip|slows}} them for {{pp|type=distance traveled|1 to 3 for 9|400 to 1000|formula=1+(0.25 per 75 units traveled)}} seconds. Enemy {{tip|champions}} hit are also inflicted with {{sti|armor penetration|{{as|20% armor reduction}}}} for 4 seconds.
|leveling = {{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|70 to 270}} {{as|(+ 100% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{st|Slow|{{ap|30 to 50}}%}}
|description2 = ''Undertow'' deals {{as|'''bonus''' physical damage}} against {{tip|monsters}}.
|leveling2    = {{st|Monster Bonus Physical Damage|{{ap|20 to 120}}|Total Monster Damage|{{ap|70+20 to 270+120}} {{as|(+ 100% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
|description3 = The axe remains in place for a duration equal to ''Undertow's'' cooldown, granting {{tip|sight}} of its surroundings for {{fd|0.5}} seconds. '''Olaf''' can pick up the axe to reduce ''Undertow's'' {{sti|'''current''' cooldown}} to {{pp|2.5 to 0 for 6|0 to 2.5|type=seconds elapsed since axe landed|formula=2.5 (affected by ability haste) - seconds}}.
|description4 = ''{{tt|Nearby monsters|100 range estimated}} are granted {{tip|ghosting}} for 5 seconds upon Undertow's cast.''
|target range = {{dv|{{tip|cr|icononly = true}} {{tt|425|Minimum missile range, estimated}}|{{tt|1000|Maximum missile range}}}}
|effect radius= {{dv|{{tip|cr|icononly = true}} {{tt|100|Impact additional radius}}|{{tt|250|Axe retrieval radius}}|{{tip|sight|icononly=true}}{{tt|300|Axe landing brief sight radius}}}}
|width        = {{tip|er|icononly = true}} {{tt|180|Missile width}}
|speed = 1600
|cooldown = 9
|cdstart  = on-cast
|cast time    = {{fd|0.25}}
|cost = {{ap|50 to 70}}
|costtype = Mana
|targeting = Location
|affects = Enemies
|damagetype = Physical
|projectile = special
|spelleffects = Aoe
|spellshield = True
|outofrange = cast at max
|notes = 
* ''Undertow'' may hit additional targets upon landing, but not targets already struck in-flight.
** The axe will land approximately 50 units further than ''Undertow's'' target range if cast below maximum range.
* Projectile-intercepting effects (e.g. {{ai|Wind Wall|Yasuo}}, {{ai|Unbreakable|Braum}}) cannot destroy the axe, they will instead cause it to stop prematurely and remain on the ground upon collision.
* The timer for how long an axe stays on the ground does not begin until it has landed, thus it is possible to throw another axe before retrieving the first.
* '''Olaf''' cannot pick up an enemy '''Olaf's''' axe on the ground.
{{Effect at cast time start}}
}}

{{{{{1<noinclude>|Ability data</noinclude>}}}|Duskbringer|{{{2|}}}|{{{3|}}}|{{{4|}}}|{{{5|}}}
|champion     = Nocturne
|skill        = Q
|icon         = Duskbringer.png
|blurb        = {{sbc|Active:}} {{ci|Nocturne}} casts out a shadow blade in the target direction that leaves a ''Dusk Trail'' in its wake, dealing {{as|physical damage}} to enemies hit. Enemy {{tip|champions}} hit will leave a ''Dusk Trail'' in their wake for a few seconds.
|blurb2      = While on the ''Dusk Trail'', Nocturne is {{tip|ghosted}} and gains {{sti|ms|{{as|'''bonus''' movement speed}}}} and {{as|{{sti|'''bonus''' attack damage}}}}.
|description  = {{sbc|Active:}} '''Nocturne''' casts out a shadow blade in the target direction that leaves a ''Dusk Trail'' in its wake, dealing {{as|physical damage}} to enemies hit. Enemy {{tip|champions}} and large {{tip|monsters}} hit will leave a ''Dusk Trail'' behind while moving. ''Dusk Trails'' last 5 seconds and will slowly disappear afterwards.
|leveling     = {{st|Physical damage|{{ap|65 to 225}} {{as|(+ 85% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
|description2 = While on the ''Dusk Trail'', '''Nocturne''' is {{tip|ghosted}} and gains {{as|{{sti|'''bonus''' attack damage}}}} and {{sti|ms|{{as|'''bonus total''' movement speed}}}}.
|leveling2    = {{st|Bonus Attack Damage|{{ap|15 to 55}}}}
{{st|Bonus Movement Speed|{{ap|20 to 40}}%}}
|range        = {{tip|cr|icononly = true}} {{tt|1200|Shadow blade missile range}}
|width        = {{tip|er|icononly = true}} {{tt|120|Shadow blade missile width}}
|speed        = 1600
|effect radius= {{tip|cr|icononly = true}} {{tt|150|Dusk Trail blob radiuses}}
|cooldown     = 8
|cost         = {{ap|60 to 80}}
|cast time    = {{fd|0.25}}
|costtype     = Mana
|targeting    = Direction
|affects      = Self, Enemies
|damagetype   = Physical
|spellshield  = True
|spelleffects = Area of effect
|projectile   = True
|notes        = 
* ''Duskbringer'' checks for and hits targets 25 units outside of the missile's maximum range.
* ''Duskbringer's'' damage is not increased by the {{as|'''bonus''' AD}} gained from its trail, meaning that casting it again while on the trail from the last cast will not result in higher damage.
** It is observed from seasons ago that this is intentionally hard-coded into the ability to avoid the projectile increasing its own damage. This feature is somewhat deprecated as it also limits chain-casting ''Duskbringer''.
* ''Duskbringer's Dusk Trail'' will expose the path of affected units until its duration ends. It is a form of {{tip|obscured vision}}; the trail indirectly reveals the location of enemy units even in the fog of war, including those shrouded by {{tip|stealth}}.
* {{tip|Spell shield}} will block the damage and also prevents the ''Dusk Trail'' from following the target.
* The formed ''Dusk Trail'' does not disappear if ''Duskbringer'' is intercepted by {{ai|Wind Wall|Yasuo}} or {{ai|Unbreakable|Braum}}.
{{Effect at cast time start}}
* The {{as|'''bonus''' movement speed}} {{tip|stacks multiplicatively}} with other sources of movement speed boosts.
}}

